@startuml
title The counter mistake, and why the order matters
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #B54A4A
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  ActorBorderColor #B54A4A
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  GroupBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
  GroupBorderColor #B54A4A
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  BorderColor #B54A4A
}

actor "Sneaky\ncustomer" as A
participant "Swap counter\n(old shop)" as SWAP
participant "Cash-in counter" as CASH
participant "Money box" as BOX

A -> SWAP : "Please swap my sticker\nfor these two new ones"
activate SWAP

SWAP -> A : hands over the two NEW stickers first
note right of A #FDEEEE
  The old sticker is still in
  the customer's pocket. For a
  moment they hold both.
end note

group The customer runs off before the clerk finishes
  A -> CASH : cashes in one new sticker
  CASH -> A : gives back a sticker the clerk\nis about to ask for
  A -> CASH : cashes in the other new sticker
  CASH -> BOX : opens the box
  BOX -> A : real money the customer\nnever paid in
end

A -> SWAP : comes back and hands over the old sticker
SWAP -> A : "All done, thank you"
deactivate SWAP

note over SWAP, BOX
  The new shop takes your old sticker FIRST,
  and only then prints the new ones. There is
  no moment where you hold both.
end note
@enduml
